    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n310" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăcaustus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκαυστος</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>incombustible;</i> hence <i>subst. m.</i> (sc.
			lapis), <i>the carbuncle</i>, since it was regarded as
			incombustible: acaustoe (i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκαυστοι</span>), <i><span class="en">Plin. 37, 7, 25, § 92</span></i>; v.
			Sill. a. h. l.</div>
